7.Chinese new year is the most important traditional festival of china, which is also called the spring festival.
  The new year's celebration begins on(涉及到具体的某一天) the Spring Festival Eve and end on the Lantern Festival.
  The Spring Festival Eve is the last day of the last month of the year of the lunar calendar and the Lantern Festival is the 15th day of the first month of the new year.
  In different places, people have different(不要使用 have difference) customs and traditions to celebrate the Spring Festival.
  However, every family will usually gather together to have a big dinner on the Spring Festival Eve.
  in order to get rid of bad luck and welcome good luck, every family will clean their houses thoroughly.
  People will stick red couplets(对联) on the door, and the theme(subject 更侧重具体讨论的话题, theme 更侧重抽象的理念和祝福) is health, fortune and good luck.
  Other activities include giving some money in red envelopes, and visiting relatives and friends and so on.
